"hadiths[340]{hadithnumber,text}:"
3075,"Kathir bin Abdullah narrated this statement of his grandfather regarding his father. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “There is no status of ``Jalab, Junab, Objection.'' saw Asim bin Ubaidullah has followed Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of Salem, in narrating it about Misrat. Hasan bin Amara has narrated from the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layli, on the authority of Sayyiduna Ali, on the authority of Sayyiduna Ali. A narrator named Abu Shiba has narrated it from Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA). A narrator named Shuba has narrated it on the authority of a Companion (whose name is not mentioned)."
3076,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade Muhakla, Mukhazara, Malamsa, Manabza and Muzabna. A narrator named `Umar (bin Yunus) narrated this. My father explained it as follows. Mukhadra means that a buyer will not buy a field or an orchard of date palms until they are red or yellow (i.e. the produce is ripe). Manabaza means that the buyer will throw the cloth to the seller and the seller will throw the cloth to the buyer and say that it is yours in exchange for it. The relationship is that the buyer will buy the goods even though he has not even seen the goods. Mohakla refers to land on rent."
3077,"Thabit bin Saeed narrates this statement of his grandfather Sayyidna Abayd bin Hamal regarding his father. He asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, for that piece of land, which he said: ""I used to go and it was Marib."" The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him that piece of land. I went to a place called Malh, in the age of Jahiliyyah, that is a place where?? There is no salt, whoever reaches there can get it. Its example is that of flowing water which does not stop flowing. Then Iqra asked Abayd about the piece of land of salt, then Sayyiduna Abayd said: I am making it with you on the condition that you will use it as charity on my behalf. Of the water flowing from the fountain, whoever reaches it will use it. The narrator narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted him some land and a date garden at the place of Jarf, meaning Jarf. Narrator named Faraj bin Saeed has narrated this. It was also the case that whoever reaches it will get it."
3078,"Mujahid narrates that a few people decided to work jointly in an agricultural land, one of them had the land, another person was to provide agricultural implements, a third person was to work in the field, and a fourth person was to provide seeds. ordered to be done, fixed the wages for the person who had to labor in the field, and declared the man who supplied you to be the owner of all the produce. The narrator narrates that I narrated this hadith to Makhool, so he said, ""I would not have been happy if I had received Wasif in exchange for this hadith."" This Hadith is transmitted by Messenger and is authentic. The narrator of this tradition is weak."
3079,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said (in Islam) there is no harm or harm to a person who tries to cause harm, Allah will afflict him with harm, and whoever tries to cause hardship, Allah will afflict him with hardship."
3080,"Abu Hab narrates that Sayyidna Faid bin Khalid said to me: Shall I read to you the text that the Prophet (peace be upon him) had written for me? (These are his words). ""This (the text is about) Faid bin Khalid bought from the Messenger of Allah, Sayyiduna Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, a slave (maybe the narrator doubts) a maidservant, in whom there is no disease, no deceit, no defect. This is a transaction of one Muslim with another Muslim. There are these words in a tradition, then he brought out this writing in front of me. ""This (the text is about) Faid bin Khalid bought from the Messenger of Allah, Sayyidna Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, a slave (maybe the narrator doubts) a maidservant (here the narrator named Ibad is doubtful) in whom there is no disease, no deceit, no defect. This is a transaction of one Muslim with another Muslim."
3081,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: When Sayyiduna Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, may Allah be pleased with him, gave a person his property as Mudarabat, he stipulated that he would not travel with it on the sea, that he would not camp with it in any (valley) place, that he would not buy any living thing with it, and if he did so, he would pay the guarantee (compensation) for it. When I mentioned it in front of the Prophet (peace be upon him), he declared it correct."
3082,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: I attended a funeral prayer in which the Prophet (PBUH) was also present. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) started to leave there. He said, ""You people, perform the funeral prayer for your companion. When Sayyiduna saw you going back, he said, 'O Messenger of God, this person is free from his debt. I am his guarantor for the payment he is responsible for.'"" May Allah give you a good reward, just as you have taken responsibility for the payment of your Muslim brother, so may Allah take responsibility for your payments on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever pays his brother's debt on the Day of Resurrection, Allah will be responsible for the payments of that person on the Day of Resurrection."
3083,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) attended a funeral. When he was placed, he was told that he was responsible for a debt. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) withdrew. Sayyidna Ali said: O Prophet of Allah, I am his guarantor. In giving a loan, the Prophet said: O Ali, may Allah meet your needs in the same way as you have met the needs of your fellow Muslim brother. Is it common for faith? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is common to all believers."
3084,"Sayyidna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a gentleman passed away, we bathed him, shrouded him, perfumed him and placed him near the place of Sayyidna Gabriel (peace be upon him), where funerals were kept. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) started turning back, one of us, whose name was Abu Qatada, asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to serve him, O Messenger of Allah, the payment of these two (dinars) is my responsibility. Allah's Messenger (may peace be upon him) performed the funeral prayer for this person. After that, whenever the Prophet (peace be upon him) met Sayyiduna Abu Qatada, the Prophet (peace be upon him) asked him what he did with these two dinars. Finally, when Sayyiduna Qatadah told the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that both of them had been fulfilled in the Messenger of Allah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Now this person has been blessed with coolness."
3085,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) quotes this statement of the Prophet (PBUH) regarding the worship of Allah, the most excellent thing to do is to gain understanding in the religion. One jurist is more of a source of trouble for Satan than a thousand worshipers. There is a pillar of everything, the pillar of this religion is Fiqh. Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I should sit for an hour and gain knowledge of religion, this is more beloved to me than that I spend the whole night performing Nawafil."
3086,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prophets are leaders, jurisprudents are chiefs, their companionship leads to increase (in knowledge and reward)."
3087,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is permissible to kill any Muslim in three cases: a married adulterer who will be stoned to death, a person who kills someone intentionally and will be killed in return, a person who leaves Islam and opposes Allah and His Messenger, then he will be killed, or crucified, or exiled."
3088,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3089,"The same tradition is also narrated in some other isnads, however, some words have been said about some of its narrators."
3090,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): By the one who has no god but a Muslim who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, shedding his blood is permissible only in three cases: when he abandons Islam and separates from the community (of Muslims), or a married adulterer and (i.e., a murderer) life for life."
3091,"This tradition is narrated from Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) along with another chain of transmission."
3092,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): It is not permissible to shed the blood of any Muslim (after this, according to the previous hadith). Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates the same as the previous tradition regarding the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
3093,"Amish says: I narrated this hadith to Ibrahim, so he said: Aswad narrated this hadith to me regarding Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her)."
3094,"A Muhaddith named Abd al-Rahman narrates: The narrator has combined these two traditions, that is, the tradition narrated by Masrooq from Sayyidna Abdullah and the tradition narrated by Ibrahim Aswad (from Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her)."
3095,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that any Muslim belonging to this Ummah can be killed for one of three reasons: A person who kills someone will be killed in retaliation, a married adulterer, a person who leaves the Jamaat (the narrator is doubtful, perhaps these are the words)."
3096,"This tradition is narrated from Sayyedah Aisha along with another chain of transmission. This tradition is suspended."
3097,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Allah Ta’ala narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep boundaries away from Muslims as much as you can."
3098,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: (Try to keep the boundaries)."
3099,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA), Sayyidna Mu'adh Bin Jabal (RA), Sayyidna Uqbah Bin Amir Jahni (RA) said: When the hadd (matter of proof) becomes doubtful before you, keep it as far away from you as possible."
3100,"Sayyiduna Salamah bin Muhibq (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A case was presented to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a man who had committed adultery with his wife's maidservant, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not issue a ban on him."
3101,"Sayyiduna Hakeem bin Hizam (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) forbade taking revenge in the mosque, establishing boundaries in it, and reciting poetry in it."
3102,"Sayyiduna Hakeem bin Hizam (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) forbade taking qisas in the mosque or establishing limits in it."
3103,"Sayyiduna Hakeem bin Hizam (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Limits should not be established in mosques and Qisas should not be taken in them."
3104,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) says: Among the children of Israel there was an order of retribution, but there was no order of death among them, so Allah said this to this Ummah (which is mentioned in the Qur'an in these words:). ""Retribution has been made obligatory upon you for the slain."" So whoever is forgiven by his brother. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, says: This forgiveness will be in such a way that the other party agrees to accept the debt in the act of murder. ""This is a relief and a mercy from your Lord."" This tradition is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) regarding Mujahid."
3105,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: When a fugitive steals a slave, his hand will not be cut off, and the hand of a dhimmi will not be cut off either. This hadith has been narrated as marfu' hadith only by Fahdnami narrator, it is true that this hadith is muquf."
3106,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, was convinced that if a fugitive slave steals, his hand will not be cut off."
3107,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, is convinced that the limit will not be extended to a slave, nor will the limit be extended to a person living in a Jewish or Christian land."
3108,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: There will be no limitation on the slave and the People of the Book. What is narrated before it as tradition, muquf, hadith is more authentic than this, the rest, Allah knows best."
3109,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Retribution can only be taken by the sword. Its narrator is Sulaiman Bin Arqam, Mutrook."
3110,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Retribution can only be taken with an iron (weapon), life or other than (an organ) can be taken only with an iron (weapon)."
3111,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Retribution can only be taken by the sword."
3112,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Retribution can only be taken with weapons."
3113,"This tradition is narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him). There is a narrator named Abu Mu'adh Sulaiman ibn Arqam, obsolete."
3114,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement on the authority of his father: A man struck another man in the knee, and that man came to the service of the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, and he said: O Messenger of God, give me retribution. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) punished him, then that person came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have become lame (so punish the other party more).” The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: I forbade you, you disobeyed me. (The narrator narrates:) After that, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that revenge should be taken on the injured person before he recovers."
3115,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person was injured and he intended to take revenge, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade taking revenge on the person who injured him, until the injured person recovers."
3116,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but there is some wording difference in it."
3117,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person struck another person in the knee, and that person came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to present Qisas (the case of taking revenge) and he said to him: You should get well first. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him, ""You will not get anything, you have disobeyed."" A narrator named Sheikh Abu Ahmad bin Abdus says: This hadith was narrated only by Abu Bakr and Uthman (both of them are the sons of Abu Shaybah). Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal and other muhaddiths have narrated this hadith from Amr (bin Dinar) on the authority of Ibn ‘Alaihi, on the authority of Ayyub. Amr ibn Dinar's disciples narrated it in the same way on his authority, and it is safe to have this tradition, Mursal."
3118,"This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (PBUH) on the authority of Muhammad bin Talha along with another chain of transmission."
3119,"Muhammad bin Talha narrated: A person shot an arrow in the leg of another, so the other person came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, give me retribution. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him retribution, then he (the person who took retribution) did not recover, so he came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Give me my right."
3120,"This tradition is narrated from Muhammad bin Talha along with another chain of transmission."
3121,"Amr bin Shu'ayb narrates this statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then forbade taking revenge for an injured person before his recovery."
3122,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""One should wait for one year to take revenge for a wound."" There is a weak and obsolete narrator named Yazid bin Ayyad."
3123,"Sayyidna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sayyidna Abul Qasim said: Whoever falsely accuses his slave of adultery, he will be punished on the Day of Judgment."
3124,"This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, Imam Bukhari (may God have mercy on him) narrated it along with his chain of transmission, all its narrators are trustworthy and hafiz."
3125,"Sayyidna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard Sayyidna Abul Qasim (may God bless him and grant him peace) say: Whoever accuses his slave of adultery (falsely) and then does not repent, that person will be punished on the Day of Resurrection."
3126,"Sayyidna Abu Hurairah (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Abul Qasim (PBUH) said to me, “When a person falsely accuses his slave of adultery and the slave is acquitted of what he has (accused), then that person will be flogged on the Day of Resurrection."
3127,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall, and, Arj, I will not be retaliated against."
3128,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman's diet will be equal to a man's diet, until it reaches one-third of a woman's diet."
3129,"Ḥamzah ibn al-Qāsim narrated to us, ʿAbbās al-Dūrī narrated to us; and Muḥammad ibn Nūḥ al-Jundaysābūrī narrated to us; and Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mālik al-Askāfī narrated to us, saying: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir al-Ṣāʾigh narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿlā ibn al-Ḥārith al-Muḥāribī narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ghaylān ibn Jāmiʿ, from ʿAlqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulaymān ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: ""Māʿiz ibn Mālik came to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, purify me.' The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: 'Woe to you! Go back, seek forgiveness from Allah, and repent to Him.' He said: He went back a short distance, then came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, purify me.' The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said the same to him. This continued until the fourth time, when the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: 'From what shall I purify you?' He said: 'From zinā (unlawful sexual intercourse).' The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, asked: 'Is he afflicted with insanity?' He was informed that he was not insane. He asked: 'Has he consumed wine?' A man stood up and smelled him but found no smell of wine on him. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: 'Are you a thayyib (one who has previously engaged in lawful sexual relations)?' He said: 'Yes.' He was then ordered to be stoned. The people were divided into two groups regarding him. One group said: 'Māʿiz has perished upon the worst of his deeds; his sin has encompassed him.' The other group said: 'Is there any repentance better than the repentance of Māʿiz? A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, placed his hand in his hand, and said: ""Kill me with stones.""' They remained in that state for two or three days. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, came to them while they were sitting. He greeted them, then sat down, and said: 'Seek forgiveness for Māʿiz ibn Mālik.' They said: 'May Allah forgive Māʿiz ibn Mālik.' The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: 'He has repented a repentance that, if it were distributed among an entire nation, it would suffice them.' Then a woman from Ghāmid, of the Azd, came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, purify me.' He said: 'Woe to you! Go back, seek forgiveness from Allah, and repent to Him.' She said: 'Do you intend to turn me back as you turned back Māʿiz ibn Mālik?' He said: 'What is that?' She said: 'She is pregnant from zinā.' He said: 'Are you a thayyib?' She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then we shall not stone you until you deliver what is in your womb.' A man from the Anṣār took responsibility for her until she gave birth. He came to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: 'The Ghāmidī woman has given birth.' He said: 'Then we shall not stone her and leave her infant small, with no one to nurse him.' A man from the Anṣār stood up and said: 'I shall take responsibility for his nursing, O Prophet of Allah.' So he stoned her."""
3130,"Abdul Jabbar bin Wail has narrated this statement of his father: In the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), if a woman was forced to commit adultery with him, he did not issue a limit to that woman, but he did issue a limit to the one who violated her. The narrator narrates: It is mentioned in it that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bequeathed this woman."
3131,"Taus narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed (the following words are in the next hadith)."
3132,"Ta'aws narrates the statement of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever is killed by mistake, or (unknowingly) killed by an arrow, it will be considered as a wrongful killing, and the death of the Prophet will be the death of a wrongful killing, and the person who was killed as a noble killing will have to be avenged."
3133,"Ta'aws narrates on the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever is killed by mistake, or is killed by a stone, or is killed by a staff, then his death will be the death of culpable homicide, and the death of a person who is killed intentionally will be retribution. Angels and all humans will be cursed, no duty or filial worship of such a person will be accepted."
3134,"Taus, quoting Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever is killed by mistake, or is hit with a stone or a stick, (and he dies), then this killing will be a mistake, and his death will be the death of the wrongful killing. A narrator named Hussain has quoted these words in excess: Allah will not accept any of his obligatory or posthumous worship."
3135,"A similar hadith has been narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, the narrator did not mention Hamza in his chain of transmission. Some narrators have quoted it from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, with reference to Taus."
3136,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Deliberate killing will be punished, but if the guardian of the deceased wishes, he can forgive it."""
3137,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: The Prophet (PBUH) said: The death of a person who is killed by hitting a stone, stick, or stick without knowing it will be the death of a guilty person. This is similar to the statement of Hamad bin Zayd."
3138,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be retribution for killing on purpose, and for killing by mistake, there will be no retribution. Whoever is killed by mistake with a stone or stick will have retribution, which will be in the form of camels of different ages."
3139,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The person who is accidentally killed by hitting a stone (the narrator doubts that these are the words) or a stick will be killed by mistake, and the person who is killed intentionally will be punished."
3140,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with him, narrates as a hadeeth: (The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said) Whoever is killed by mistake or is killed by hitting him with a stone or a stick, his death will be the death of a wrongful killing, and the person who is killed intentionally will be punished. Yanaful worship will not be accepted."
3141,"Ta'aws narrates: A person who is killed by a stick, a stick, or a stone during a fight will be paid his dowry, but he will not be killed in return, because it is not known who is his killer. I say this: Have you not seen the decision of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the case of two women belonging to the Huzail tribe, one of them had killed the other with a stick. This hadith has been narrated by the son of Taus on the authority of his father."
3142,": The sons of Taos narrate this about their father: My father had a book, which contained various types of almsgiving orders, which were revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through revelation. The act of committing murder shall be the act of culpable homicide, such as by means of a stone, a cane, or a lathi (a murder is committed) while the murderer has not raised a weapon."
3143,"The sons of Taos narrate this statement of their father: A person who is accidentally killed by a stone, a lathi, his death will be miserable."
3144,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, the day of suspected murder is like the day of murder, except that the killer will not be killed."
3145,"Sayyiduna Abu Shureeh Kaabi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: (The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared Makkah Haram. No one who believes in Allah and the Last Day should shed blood in it and cut down its trees. Daya, for me it was also declared halal for a short time, then it will remain Haram until the Day of Judgment is established, O people of Khuza'ah tribe, you killed a person from Huzail tribe, I will give him death."
3146,"The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it has these words: O people of Khuza'ah tribe, you killed a person of Huzail Qila, I will pay his dowry. Whoever is killed after that, the deceased's survivors will have one of two options: if they like, they will kill (the murderer as revenge) and if they like, they will receive dowdy."
3147,"Sayyiduna Abu Shareeh Al-Khuza’i (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: “Whoever is killed or is afflicted with khabl, (says the narrator) khabl means ‘arj (i.e. becoming lame), then he will have the option of one of three things. If he takes one of these forms and then commits adultery after that, he will go to hell where he will remain forever."
3148,"Sayyiduna Abu Shareeh Al-Khuza’i (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most disliked of His creatures in the sight of Allah is the person who kills someone unjustly, and the person who demands the blood of the age of ignorance, and the person who shows his eyes in sleep what they did not see (i.e. narrates a false dream)."
3149,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) conquered Makkah, he stood in front of the people to give a sermon. After praising Allah, he said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty did not allow elephants to enter Makkah, but He gave dominion over it to His Messenger and the believers. It was not lawful for anyone before me, and it was declared lawful for me in a certain part of the day, and it will not be lawful for anyone after me. The game here will not be chased away, the tree here will not be cut, the fallen object here will not be picked up, but it can be picked up to make an announcement, to someone who is dear to him. If he is killed, he will have the option of one of two things, either he should be paid a dowry or he should be killed (as revenge), then Sayyiduna Abbas stood up and said, O Messenger of Allah: Allow us to cut the grass called Azhar, because we use it in our houses and graves. A gentleman named Abu Shah, who belonged to Yemen, said: O Messenger of Allah! Write it to me, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, write it to Abu Shah. A narrator named Walid narrates: I asked Imam Uza'i: What is meant by this sentence (of Sayyidna Abu Shah)? Write it to me! So he said: That is the sermon that he heard from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
3150,"This tradition is narrated from Imam Uza'i along with another chain of transmission."
3151,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The people of Khuza'ah tribe killed a member of the tribe in revenge for one of their slain in the year of the conquest of Makkah. ""Allah did not allow elephants to enter Makkah, but He gave His Messenger and the believers dominion over it. It was not lawful for anyone before me, and it will not be lawful for anyone after me. Remember! It became lawful for me also up to a certain part of the day, now at this time it is Haram, the thorn here cannot be broken, the tree here cannot be cut, the fallen object here cannot be picked up, but it can be picked up to announce, if a person's loved one is killed, then he will have the option of one of two things either to kill the killer (in Qisas) or to pay the dowry to the relatives of the slain. (The narrator narrates) A man from Yemen came and said: O Messenger of Allah, write it down for me, so the Prophet said: Write it down to Abu So-and-So. A man from Quraysh said: O Messenger of Allah, allow me to cut the azhar, because we use it in our houses and graves."
3152,"Malik Ishtar narrates: I attended the service of Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with him. I said: O Commander of the Faithful! When we got up from you, we heard some things, did the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) give you anything other than the Qur'an? Then Sayyiduna Ali (RA) said: No, it is only this scripture that is in the hilt of my sword. Then Sayyiduna Ali (RA) called the maidservant and she brought this scripture (it had this writing: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Surely Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him) declared Makkah Haram, and I declare Madinah Haram, between the rocky land on both sides (Madinah Munawarah) is Haram. The thorn here cannot be broken, the prey here cannot be chased away. Whoever invents any heresy or harbors any heresy, Allah will curse him with his angels and all the people. Compared to others, all believers are like a hand, their blood is of equal importance. If they are pregnant, the shelter given by an ordinary person will be recognized and no Muslim can be killed in revenge of an infidel."
3153,"Abu Huhaifa has narrated the same on the authority of Sayyiduna Ali, his words are slightly different, but the meaning is the same."
3154,"Musa bin Ali narrates: I have cursed my father during the caliphate of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) on the occasion of Hajj (reciting these verses) in a loud voice. ""O people! A wrong situation came before me that a blind person would pay the death of a sighted person, when they both fell together and both were injured. It happened that a blind person was accompanying the blind man, they both fell into a well, and the blind man fell on top of the blind man, as a result of which the blind man died, so Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, gave this decision, the blind man will pay the death of the blind man."
3155,"Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, he has committed adultery with such and such a woman. He also mentioned the woman’s name. (i.e.) did not punish him)."
3156,"Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: During the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a girl became pregnant as a result of adultery. He was asked: Who made you pregnant? He said: I have been impregnated by Al-Muqaad (namely Sahib). When he was asked about this, he confessed his crime. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He will not be able to bear the whip. So, under the order of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he took 100 twigs and gave him a single blow. The narrator has described it in the same way, but it is true that it is narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Umamah bin Sahl (RA)."
3157,"Sayyidna Abu Umamah bin Sahl (RA) narrates this on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri (RA): A man named Anjat lived near the house of Sayyidna Sa’d (RA), he committed adultery with a woman. Imam Dar Qutni says: (In this hadith, the word Ikhtal is used), but the correct word is Ishkal, (i.e. palm branches)."
3158,"Sayyidna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates this statement of Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri Radiyallahu Anhu: The stomach of a Sahib called Anus was slightly enlarged. He lived near the house of Umm Saad. A girl became pregnant."
3159,"Sayyiduna Abu Umamah bin Sahl (RA) narrates the statement of his father: A maidservant of Banus Sa'ida became pregnant as a result of adultery, and when she gave birth to a child, he asked her: ""Whose child is your child?"" He replied: So, he (the accused) was a thin and weak person, his skin was like that of a snake due to weakness. Lo, which has a hundred branches, and he struck it once, so did the people."
3160,"Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who had become pregnant as a result of adultery. The clothes were tied well and then she was stoned. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed her funeral prayer. It was submitted to him that he first stoned her to death and then performed her funeral prayer. Who sacrifices himself (in obedience to Allah's command)."
3161,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: You have stoned him, (and now offered the funeral prayer). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If all the people of Madinah did this repentance, it would be enough for them all."
3162,"Sayyiduna Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A woman from the tribe of Jahaina came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
3163,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A thief was brought to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who had stolen a cloak. The people said: O Messenger of Allah, he has stolen. The thief said: O Messenger of Allah, yes, the Prophet said, take him and cut off his hand, then apply a scar (so that the blood will flow) and then bring him to me. Accepted."
3164,"Muhammad Bin Abd al-Rahman narrates: A thief was brought to the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him) who had stolen a cloak. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Have you really stolen? He said yes. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: cut off his hand and put a scar on it. The people cut off his hand and then put a scar on it."
3165,"Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman has narrated a similar tradition from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him)."
3166,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When a person steals, his right hand should be cut off. If he steals again, his left foot should be cut off. If he steals again, I will imprison him and keep him in prison until he recovers. having no feet by which to walk."
3167,"Maysara narrated: A man and his mother came to the service of Sayyiduna Ali, the woman said: This son of mine has killed my husband. Tubita said: (The murdered) was my slave, who committed adultery with my mother. Hazrat Ali said, ""You are both disgraced and lost. (O woman) If you are truthful, your son will be killed, and if your son is truthful, we will stone you."" When Sayyiduna Ali went to pray, the boy said to his mother: What do you think they will kill me or stone you? The narrator says: Then both of them left. When Sayyiduna Ali (RA) finished praying, he inquired about them and was told that they had both left."
3168,"Uqbah bin Aws narrates this statement of a Companion: On the occasion of the conquest of Makkah, when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah, he said: ""There is no god but Allah, He is the One God. He fulfilled His promise, He helped His servant, He drove back the armies (of enemies). Remember, everything that is considered great and excellent (in society) and counted (every) blood (retribution) and wealth (i.e. payment) is under these two feet of mine (i.e. I give it to him). I consider it forbidden) except for the service of Baitullah and the service of giving water to the pilgrims (because these will be the standard of virtue) Remembering that murder is suspected of intentional, if someone is killed with a stick or staff, his death is a hundred camels, of which forty will be pregnant she-camels."
3169,"This tradition along with some other isnaads has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr."
3170,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: On the occasion of the conquest of Makkah, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “There is no god but Allah, He is the One God, He fulfilled His promise, He helped His servant, He drove back the armies (of the enemies) Remember, everything that is considered great (and virtue) and is counted (in society).” Every) blood (retribution) and property (i.e. payment) of Jahiliyyah is under these two feet of mine (i.e. I declare it forbidden) except the service of the House of Allah and the service of giving water to the pilgrims (because these will be the standard of virtue). Dit is a hundred camels."
3171,"Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aws narrates this on the authority of a Sahabi: When the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Makkah (after that he narrated the hadith as mentioned above)."
3172,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the House of Ka'b while standing on the steps. ""All praise is due to Allah who fulfilled His promise, helped His servants, drove back the armies (of the disbelievers) Remember, the victim of wrongdoing is the one who is killed by a stick or a staff, his body will be a hundred camels, in which forty camels will be pregnant. is below (i.e. I abrogate them) except (two things) the service of the Ka'ba and the service of giving water to the pilgrims."
3173,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying this while standing on the steps of the Kaaba (after that he mentioned the above hadith)."
3174,"Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that retribution can only be done with the sword."
3175,"Hasan al-Basri narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that revenge can only be taken by the sword. A narrator named Yunus narrates: I asked Hassan Basri: From whom did you hear this hadith? So he replied, I have heard Sayyidna Numan bin Basheer (RA) mentioning this."
3176,"Sayyidna Nu'man bin Basheer (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Everything (killing by means of a sword) is considered as a wrongful killing, and in wrongful killings (death) is required. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3177,"Sayyidna Nu'man bin Basheer (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Everything (killing by means of a sword) is considered as a wrongful killing, and in wrongful killings (death) is required."
3178,"Sayyidna Nu'man bin Basheer (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Anything (killed by means of) other than iron (weapon) will be considered as wrongful killing, and for wrongful killings (death) will be required."""
3179,"The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyidna Nu'man bin Bashir (RA)."
3180,"Sayyidna Nu'man bin Basheer (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Anything (killed by means of) other than iron (weapon) will be considered as wrongful killing, and for wrongful killings (death) will be required."""
3181,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Qisas will be taken only when a person is killed by the sword, and in the case of wrongful killing (payment of dowry) will be imposed on the family of the murderer. It is narrated in the same way on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri (RA)."
3182,"Ikrimah narrates: Sayyidna Ali (RA) burned some people who were apostates. Sayyidna Ibn Abbas was informed about this, so he said: I do not burn those people in the fire, because the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this: Do not punish anyone (i.e. by burning them in fire) in the same way that Allah punishes them. (Sayyidna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him) said, ""I would have killed those people because the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said this: ""Whoever changes his religion (i.e. Islam), kill him."" The narrator narrates: When Sayyiduna Ali (RA) was informed about this, he said, May Ibn Abbas (RA) be satyanas. This tradition is proven and correct."
3183,"Bashir bin Yasar narrates about Sayyidna Sahl bin Abu Hatmah (RA) and Hazrat Muhaisah Bin Mas’ud (RA): These two men went to Khabeer. In those days, peace (of Muslims and Jews) was going on. These two men separated from each other in relation to their work. Sayyidna Muhaisah (RA) reached his other companion, Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Sahl, who was covered in blood and had been killed. Muhaisa buried him later when they came to Madinah, Abdul Rahman bin Sahl, Hawaisah bin Masood and Muhaisah bin Masud attended the Prophet’s service. Abdul Rahman bin Sahl started talking. Willing to take the blood of his partner (in exchange, the narrator suspects, perhaps these are the words) to become worthy of the blood of his murderer? He said: O Messenger of Allah, how can we take an oath? While we were not there, we did not see (the killings)? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Fifty of the Jews will be acquitted after taking an oath."" The narrator narrates: So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid these people on his behalf."
3184,"Bashir bin Yasar, the freed slave of Banu Haritha, who was an elderly and wise man, and he also visited some of the Companions belonging to his (master's) family of Banu Haritha, including Sayyidna Rafi' bin Khadij, may Allah be pleased with him, Sayyidna Sahl bin Abu Hatmah, may God be pleased with him, and Sayyidna Suwayd bin Nu'man may Allah be pleased with him. About the Banu Haritha, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Sahl, a member of the Ansar, was killed in Khyber. Bashir mentioned this: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Sahl (RA) and Sayyidna Muhaisa Bin Mas’ud (RA) belonged to Banu Haritha. These two men visited Khyber during the time of the Holy Prophet (PBUH). In those days, there was peace (between Muslims and Jews), only Jews lived in Khyber. After that, he has narrated the hadith as mentioned above) but it contains these words: How can we accept the oaths of the people of the infidels?"
3185,"Basheer bin Yasar narrates this on the authority of Sayyiduna Sahl bin Abu Hatmah (RA) and Hadhrat Rafi’ bin Khadij (RA): Both of them have narrated this: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Sahl (RA) and Sayyidna Muhaisah (RA) went to Khyber after that, according to the previous hadith."
3186,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: Sayyidna Muhaisah bin Masoud (RA), Sayyidna Hawaisa bin Masoud (RA), Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman RA (Bin Sahl) and Sayyidna Abdullah Sahl (RA) went to Khyber. When told about this, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them, “You can make fifty people take an oath as a measure of mercy and punish your murderer, so these gentlemen did not like it. O Messenger of Allah, should we accept the oaths of the infidels? (The narrator narrates) Then the wealth of Zakat came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) himself paid the death of (the deceased)."
3187,"Bashir bin Yasar narrates: A companion from the Ansar, whose name was Sayyidna Sahl bin Abu Hatmah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated this, he went to Khaibar along with some members of his tribe, there they were separated from each other, then they found one of their members killed. So those people said: We did not kill, nor do we know about the murderer. Then these gentlemen came to the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. They said, O Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace! When we went to Khyber, we found one of our people killed, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Give the elder a chance first."" They said: We do not have any evidence. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then (those Jews) take an oath (and they will be acquitted). They said: We will not agree to the Jews taking an oath. The narrator narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not like that the blood of the deceased should go in vain, so he himself paid one hundred camels from the Zakat camels as a dowry."
3188,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3189,"Sayyiduna Sahl bin Abu Hatmah (may God be pleased with him) narrates: Some of the members of the Ansar went to Khaibar and one of them was killed. This matter came before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: ""Where are your proofs?"" He said: ""We do not have any proof."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Then take an oath.” He said, “We were not there."
3190,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): It is necessary for the claimant to present evidence and for the one who denies it, it is necessary to take an oath, but the ruling of Qasamat is different."
3191,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this saying of the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, regarding his father and his grandfather, It is necessary for the claimant to present evidence and for the one who denies it, it is necessary to take an oath, but the ruling of Qasamat is different."
3192,"The same tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, Abdul Razzaq, on the contrary, has quoted it as a Mursal tradition."
3193,"Abd al-Malik bin Umayr narrates: I was present with Sayyidna Ali, a man from Banu Ajl was brought to him, Mastward bin Qubaysa, who had left Islam and became a Christian. Sayyidna Ali asked him what I have been told about you. What have you been told about me, he asked? Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I have been told about you that you have become a Christian. He said: I am steadfast in the religion of Sayyiduna Masih (peace be upon him). Sayyiduna Ali (may peace be upon him) said to him: I am also steadfast in the religion of Sayyiduna Masih (peace be upon him). So I did not understand what the man answered. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered: Kill him, he was killed (says the narrator)."
3194,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: There was a woman who had two sons who were like pearls. She used to be rude in honor of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The man forbade her, but she did not stop. took it and stabbed that woman in the stomach (by which the woman died when this case came to the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace), then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, ""Be a witness, the blood of this woman was wasted."" These words are from a narrator named Ibn Karamat."
3195,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrates: A blind man whose mother used to insult the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the evening, that person forbade the woman but she did not stop. The blind man stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am the owner of this woman. She was insolent in honor of you. I stopped her but she did not stop. He said, you people be witnesses, the blood of this woman was wasted."
3196,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep the limits (of information) to your limit, when it reaches me, it will be necessary (to issue it)."
3197,"The same hadith is narrated along with another document, but it contains these words: ""When (the case of limitation) is brought before me, it will be necessary (to issue it)."" Muslim and Ibn Ayyash agree in narrating this tradition as, received, while Abd al-Razzaq narrated it as, mursal, tradition, followed by Ibn 'Alaihi."
3198,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: (After this there is a similar hadith)."
3199,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Forgive each other before bringing the limits to me, for the limit (of the case) that reaches me will be necessary to release (the limit). (This hadith is transmitted)."
3200,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Kill the person who changes his religion (Islam)."
3201,"Ikramah has narrated the same from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA)."
3202,"Saeed bin Abdul Aziz narrates: Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) killed a woman named Umm Qarfa Fazaria as an apostate because of her apostasy. Sayyida Umm Waraqa Ansariyyah, who was named Shaheedah by the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, was killed by the slave and maidservant of this woman during the caliphate of Sayyidna Umar, so Sayyidna Umar killed them both by crucifixion."
3203,"The same hadith along with another chain of transmission is related to Sayyiduna Umar."
3204,"Sayyiduna Jundab al-Khair (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said, ""The punishment for a sorcerer is to be killed by the sword."""
3205,"Jundab narrated about lightning: He killed a sorcerer who was with Walid bin Uqbah, then he recited this verse: Atatun al-Sahar waantum al-Taramin."
3206,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed the payment of a slave or a horse or a mule for the loss of a child in the womb. One of the parties against whom the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had given judgment said: Shall I pay his dowry? He who has neither eaten nor drunk nor uttered a sound nor wept, such blood flows into the blood, then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""He is speaking like poets, a slave or a horse or a mule must be paid as a ransom."""
3207,"Narrated by Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, inquired from the people: What was the decision of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the (disposal) of the child in the womb? As for the child in the womb, he decreed that a Yakinese slave should be paid as ransom, and the woman (slayer) should be killed in exchange for the woman. There are these words in a hadith: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) asked the people: What was the decision of the Prophet (PBUH) regarding the (disposal) of the child in the womb? So Sayyidna Hamal bin Malik bin Nabagha Ansari stood up and killed my two wives. One of them hit the other with a piece of wood. He hit her on the head with that piece of wood, as a result of which the other woman and the child in her womb died. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed about the child in the womb that a slave would be paid as a ransom, and the woman (killer) would be killed in exchange for the woman. A narrator named Ibn Junayd has narrated these words: Atarb bin Malik Yashayd Hamal bin Malik stood up (i.e. the narrator is in doubt about his name)."
3208,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: He was present when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a decision about this. Hamal bin Nabagha Ansari came and told that there was a fight between two women. The narrator (Ibn Juraj) narrates: I inquired from Amr (bin Dinar), the son of Taus did not tell me this about his father, so Amr bin Dinar said: You have made me doubt."
3209,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrated: Sayyidna Umar (RA) stood on the pulpit and said: I give the intercessor of Allah to the person who has heard the decision of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) regarding the killing of the child in the womb. I was between two women, one of them hit the other with a stick and killed the other woman and the child in her womb. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decided to pay the dowry of the child in the womb to a slave or a woman. Sayyiduna Umar said: Allahu Akbar, if we had not heard this hadith, we would have given a different decision."
3210,"The sons of Taus narrate this on the authority of their father: Sayyiduna Umar (may God be pleased with him) asked for advice (followed by a previous hadith containing these words), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the payment of a woman's dowry, and ordered the payment of a slave or a horse as a ransom for a child in the womb."
3211,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: When a woman becomes an apostate, she should not be killed. The narrator of this tradition is Abdullah bin Isa, a liar, he has quoted false traditions regarding Affan and other narrators, and there is no valid tradition related to this from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
3212,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) used to say about an apostate woman, she will be imprisoned, she will not be killed."
3213,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: A woman who apostates from Islam will be imprisoned, she will not be killed."
3214,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: On the occasion of the Battle of Uhud, a woman became apostate, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her to repent."
3215,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A woman named Umm Marwan apostatized from Islam, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that Islam be offered to her if she accepted Islam again, otherwise she would be killed."
3216,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3217,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about a woman who left Islam and became an apostate: She should be slaughtered."
3218,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: A woman apostatized from Islam, then the Prophet (PBUH) ordered people to accept Islam before her."
3219,"Zahri says about a woman who disbelieves after accepting Islam: She was told to repent: she will go, if she repents then it is fine, otherwise she will be killed."
3220,"Ibrahim Nakhai says this about the apostate woman: She was told to repent: Go, if she repents then it is fine, otherwise she will be killed."
3221,"Ibrahim Nakhai says: If that woman accepts Islam then it is fine, otherwise she will be killed."
3222,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Every apostate who does not accept Islam again will be killed, whether he is a man or a woman."
3223,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, Sayyidna Muadh bin Jabal may Allah be pleased with him, and Sayyidna Uqbah bin Amir Jahni may Allah be pleased with him say: When the matter of the hadd (to be established) becomes doubtful before you, you should fulfill the hadd as far as possible (i.e., avoid issuing it)."
3224,"Yahya bin Abd al-Rahman narrates this statement of his grandfather: On the occasion of the Battle of Khyber, the roasted meat of a goat was offered to the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, which was mixed with poison. This meat was presented as a gift by a Jewish woman. Allah's Messenger passed away, when he passed away, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called this Jewish woman. He replied, I have fed you with poison. I thought that if you really became the Prophet, it would not harm you, because Allah would fulfill His decision regarding you, (i.e., you will live until Islam prevails) and if you did not become the Prophet, then I wished to save the people from you, so he was crucified under the order of the Prophet."
3225,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: The Holy Prophet (PBUH) said to Sayyidna Ma'adh (RA) May you touch it? He said no. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'You have committed adultery.' He said, 'Yes.'"
3226,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says, when Sayyidna Ma'ez bin Malik (RA) appeared before the Prophet (PBUH) and confessed adultery before him, the Prophet (PBUH) said to Sayyidna Ma'az, ""Perhaps you only kissed, or only touched?"" They said no. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""So it is like that (that is, you have committed adultery)."" A narrator named Ibn Sinan quoted these words: Perhaps you have kissed, you have touched, remember? He did not ask. The narrator narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him, ""Did you do this (i.e. adultery)?"" (The narrator narrates) The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not use any sarcasm, so he said yes."
3227,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person from the tribe of Islam who came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who had committed adultery, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him, “Perhaps you have only kissed, or only touched, or only seen."
3228,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: A woman came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and she said: I have committed adultery, you should issue a ban on me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Bring someone who can be a sponsor for your child."" A person stood up and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, may I become a sponsor for his child?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) stoned this woman to death."
3229,"Sha'bi narrated: A married adulterer was brought before Sayyidna Ali (RA), and Sayyidna Ali (RA) flogged her on Thursday, and stoned her on Friday."
3230,"Sha'bi narrated: The maidservant of Saeed bin Qays was brought to the service of Sayyidna Ali, who had committed adultery. Sayyidna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, flogged her and then stoned her."
3231,"Sha'bi narrated: Sayyiduna Ali (RA) flogged him on Thursday and stoned him to death on Friday. So he said, I have flogged him according to the order of the Book of Allah and stoned him according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah."
3232,"Sha'bi narrated: The maidservant of Saeed bin Qays was brought to the service of Sayyidna Ali, who had committed adultery. Sayyidna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, flogged her and then stoned her."
3233,"Narrated Sha'bi: A woman called Sharaha Hamdaniyyah was brought before Sayyiduna Ali, (a woman) who had committed adultery, so Sayyidna Ali sent her back to give birth to the first child. He stoned her and said, ""I have flogged her according to the order of the Book of Allah, and I have stoned her according to the order of the Sunnah."" Hazrat Ali said, ""If a woman gives birth to an illegitimate child or confesses to it, the Imam will stone her first, then others will stone her, but the woman whose crime is proven by witnesses will be stoned first by the witnesses, then others will stone her."""
3234,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: When you find someone doing the deeds of the people of Lut, then kill both the person doing the deed and the one with whom the deed was done."
3235,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, says about such a virgin who is caught doing the deeds of the people of Lot: He will be stoned."
3236,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When a person says to another person, O eunuch, beat (the person who said) twenty sticks. kill"
3237,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that whoever misbehaves with an animal, kill him and kill that animal as well. The narrator says: We said to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas: What is the animal's fault? So he said, ""I did not hear these words from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, but I think that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, disapproved of eating the meat of the animal on which this act was performed, or gaining any profit from it."""
3238,"Sayyidina Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates: A woman from the tribe of Jahaina came to the service of the Prophet (SAW) and she confessed to adultery. He said to (this woman) you go and breastfeed the child. This woman did so, then she came to the service of the Holy Prophet, upon the order of the Holy Prophet, the clothes were tied tightly on her body, then under his order, she was stoned. Peace be upon him said: This woman has repented like this, if it is distributed among seventy people of Madinah, it will be enough for all of them."
3239,"Sayyiduna Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the same thing: However, it contains these words."
3240,"Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: A member of the tribe of Islam came to the Prophet (PBUH) and confessed to adultery. The Prophet (PBUH) turned away from him. He confessed, and the Prophet (PBUH) reprimanded him. He testified about himself four times (that he had committed adultery). The Prophet said, ""Are you mad?"" He said, ""No, Prophet."" Allah's Messenger inquired if you are married, he said yes, then he was stoned to death in Eid Gah under the order of the Holy Prophet (SAW)."
3241,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, prescribed one-third of the death penalty for removing the eye of a blind person from its designated place, and one-third of the death penalty for amputating the hand of a person with a paralyzed hand."
3242,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribed a dowry of one hundred camels. Narrator narrates: He fixed the price of Haravant at eighty dirhams, so the total amount of the diet was eight thousand dirhams, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set the diet of the People of the Book as half of the diet of a Muslim. During the time of the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) and during the caliphate of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, this was the same amount. During the caliphate of Sayyiduna Umar, camels became expensive, so Sayyiduna Omar fixed their price at twenty-two dirhams (per camel), so the amount of diyat increased to 12,000 dirhams."
3243,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to a Dhimmi by paying the same amount of money as a Muslim."
3244,"Ibn Shahab narrates: Both Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (RA) and Sayyidna Umar (RA) set the same rate of diet for a Jewish Christian person as that of a free Muslim person, provided that person is a covenant (i.e. Dhimmi), while Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani and Sayyidna Muawiya (RA) did not give diet to a polytheist Muslim."
3245,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had decided to pay twelve thousand dirhams in the Dayat. A narrator named Muhammad bin Maimon narrates: Our teacher narrated it to us once on the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), however, most of the times he has quoted this tradition as a (messenger) tradition from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding Ikrimah."
3246,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: During the time of the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, a person killed another person, so the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, set his death penalty at twelve thousand dirhams. ""Except in the case that Allah and His Messenger make them rich with His grace"" means those people will be rich by receiving money."
3247,"Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The diet of a Jew and a Christian will be 4,4,000 dirhams, while the diet of a Magian will be 800 dirhams."
3248,"Saeed bin Musayyib narrates: Sayyiduna Umar (RA) fixed the diet of a Jew and a Christian at four thousand dirhams and the diet of a Magian at eight hundred dirhams."
3249,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: These two things were found in the possession of the sword of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The most disobedient person on earth is the one who kills someone other than his killer (the narrator doubts perhaps these are the words), who kills someone other than his killer, and the person who attributes himself to someone else instead of his master. Obligatory worship will not be accepted. (The second thing is this): The lives of the believers are of equal status and the protection given to them by the common person will be respected, no Muslim will be killed in exchange for an unbeliever, and no covenant (dhimmi) will be killed, and people belonging to two religions will not inherit Ekad Wasra (this tradition is short)."
3250,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) forbade his companions to be gentle with the Khawarij. They passed by Abdullah bin Khabab, so they seized him and took him and left. They passed by a date that had fallen from a tree. Abdullah bin Khabab said: Shall I not guide you to something that is more honorable for you? The people said: Yes. Abdullah bin Khabab said: I am he. Then these people killed Abdullah bin Khabab. Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was informed of this, so he sent a message to the people: Pay us the death of Abdullah bin Khabab. What is killing? Sayyiduna Ali said, Have you all killed him? They replied, Yes, then Sayyiduna Ali (RA) said Allahu Akbar: Then he ordered, (your companions) to attack these people vigorously. The narrator narrates: So Sayyidna Ali (RA) killed all these people, Sayyidna Ali (RA) ordered to find the one with protruding flesh among them. After that, the narrator has mentioned the whole incident."
3251,"Abu Huws narrates: On the day of the battle of Nahrwan, we were with Sayyidna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) on one side of the canal, while foreigners came and camped on the other side of the canal. If you heard, Abdullah bin Khabab said, My father narrated this hadith to me. He heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: ""Such a trial will come. A sitting person will be better than a standing one, and a standing person will be better than a running one."" So they said: Allah said: Call them loudly and tell them to send the killer of Abdullah bin Khabab to us. In response, these people said three times: We have all killed them. Then Sayyiduna Ali (RA) said to his companions: Now attack them. The narrator narrates: After that Sayyiduna Ali and his companions killed those people. The narrator narrates."
3252,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: A free person will not be killed in exchange for a slave."
3253,"Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) say: When a free person kills a slave as a premeditated murder, then qisas will not be taken, but the dowry shall be paid. (Imam Darqutni (may God have mercy on him) says:) This hadith cannot be presented as evidence, because it, the Messenger, is."
3254,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Sunnah (injunction) is: A Muslim should not be killed in exchange for an infidel, the Sunnah (injunction) is that a free person should not be killed in exchange for a slave."
3255,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: Sayyiduna Abu Bakr and Sayyiduna Umar did not kill a free man (as revenge) for killing a slave."
3256,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3257,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Sunnah (ruling) is this: A Muslim shall not be killed in exchange for a contract (i.e. a non-Muslim), and a free person shall not be killed in exchange for a slave."
3258,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said about the killing of a slave of a free person: In it the price (as dowry) will be paid."
3259,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had a Muslim killed in return for an agreement (Dhimmi). This hadith has been narrated only by Ibrahim bin Abu Yahya as a Musnad. This person is an abandoned hadith. It is true that this tradition has been narrated by Ibn Belmani as a transmitted tradition."
3260,"Abd al-Rahman bin Belmani, quoted, has narrated this as a hadith: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a Muslim killed in Qisas, that Muslim had killed a Jew. Ramadi has quoted these words: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) killed a Muslim in exchange for a dhimmi."
3261,"Abd al-Rahman bin Belmani narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) killed a person belonging to the people of Qiblah in exchange for a dhimmi. He said, ""I have the most right to fulfill my duty."""
3262,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3263,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Amlak (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put stitches in the eyes of those (the apostates) because they put stitches in the eyes of the shepherd (of the camels of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)). Ibn Sa'eed says that by these (the apostates) are meant the people of the ``Arina'' tribe."
3264,"Sayyidina Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Khurash bin Umayyah (a non-Muslim) was killed, although the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had already forbidden killing a non-Muslim. (The narrator narrates) This happened when Khurash bin Umayyah killed a man from the Hazail tribe on the occasion of the conquest of Makkah."
3265,"Sayyiduna Asma Bin Malik (RA) narrates: During the time of the Holy Prophet (SAW), a slave stole something. His case was presented to the Prophet (SAWS) and the Prophet (SAWS) forgave him. Then his case was presented to the Prophet (SAWS) a second time that he had stolen, and the Prophet (SAWS) forgave it again. Then for the fourth time, the case was presented to you that he had stolen? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forgave him again, then when he was accused of stealing for the fifth time, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off one of his hands. The narrator narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""It is four (times of forgiveness) instead of four (times of forgiveness)."
3266,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: This verse, warriors?? Revealed about: ""Indeed, those who fight Allah and His Messenger: this is their punishment."" When those people commit the crime of robbing and killing people and taking property, they will be crucified. If they kill people but do not take property, they will be killed."
3267,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: Sayyidna Ali Radiyallahu Anhu passed away from a mad woman of the so-and-so tribe who had committed adultery and Sayyiduna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu ordered her to be stoned. ""The pen has been lifted from three types of people, a madman whose intellect has been overwhelmed, a person who sleeps until he wakes up and a child until he becomes an adult."" So Sayyiduna Umar (RA) said: You; He said correctly: Yes, then Sayyiduna Umar (RA) left this woman."
3268,"Saeed bin Musaib narrates: Two men were brought to the service of the Holy Prophet, one of whom had killed and the other had held (the slain), so the Holy Prophet had the murderer killed (as a punishment), and the one who held (the slain) was imprisoned."
3269,"Ismail Ibn Umayyah, Marfu', narrates as a hadith: The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: The one who kills will be killed and the one who holds the slain will be imprisoned."
3270,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) said, ""When a person is holding someone and another kills him, the person who killed him will be killed, and the person holding him will be imprisoned."""
3271,"Ismail Ibn Umayyah narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave this decision in a case in which one person held another captive, and the third person killed him."
3272,"Amir (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) also made the same decision"
3273,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Qatadah bin Abdullah: If I had not heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The revenge of the children will not be taken from the father, then I would have killed you (the narrator doubts that perhaps these are the words) I would have blown your neck."
3274,"Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) says: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying that a father will not be retaliated against his son."
3275,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No limit will be established in the mosque and no father will be killed in exchange for the son."
3276,"Narrated Umar: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that the father will not be killed in exchange for the son."
3277,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""The father will not be killed in exchange for the son, even if (the father killed the son) intentionally."""
3278,"Sayyidna Saraqa bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): We will take revenge from the son for the father, but we will not take revenge for the son from his father."
3279,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): No boundary shall be established in the mosque and no father shall be killed in exchange for the son."
3280,"The same tradition is also narrated along with another document, however, these words are added in it: father will not be avenged by son."
3281,"Sayyiduna Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, ""The son will not be retaliated against by the father."""
3282,"Amr bin Shu'ayb, on the authority of his father, narrates the following statement of his grandfather: A man killed his slave as premeditated murder, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flogged him and exiled him for a year."
3283,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: A man was brought to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who killed his slave as a premeditated murder, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flogged him and exiled him for a year."
3284,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3285,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3286,"Amr Bin Shuaib narrates: For a Muslim who kills a person of the Book, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has made it necessary to pay four thousand dirhams (as a ransom)."
3287,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, the Dhimmi's diet will be equal to the Muslim's diet. This hadith has not been narrated by anyone other than Abukarz regarding Nafi, and this person is abandoned, his name is Abdullah bin Abd al-Malik Fahri."
3288,"Sayyiduna Osama bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has declared the contract (Dhimmi) to be equal to the Muslim's. Uthman is a narrator, waqasi, and obsolete hadith."
3289,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A Muslim killed a dhimmi as a premeditated murder. This case was brought before Sayyidna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), so he did not kill him (the murderer as retribution), and he (the murdered person) was sentenced to death, which was the same as the death of a Muslim."
3290,"Saeed bin Musayyib narrates: Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) fixed the diet of a Jew and a Christian at 4,000 dirhams, while a Magian set it at 800 dirhams. Shuba says: I asked my teacher, have you heard this hadith from Saeed himself? He answered no! By the way, if I wanted, I could have listened to it in his own words. This hadith was narrated to me by Thabit Haddad. Shuba says: Then I met Thabit Haddad and he narrated this hadith to me."
3291,"Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The diet of a Jew and a Christian will be four thousand dirhams, while the diet of a Magian will be eight hundred dirhams."
3292,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3293,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that considering someone as a partner of Allah does not make someone (a person) immune. The narrator named Afif bin Salem has been misled in quoting this hadith as a hadeeth, it is correct, this hadeeth has been narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar as his saying."
3294,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: A person who takes someone as a partner of Allah will not be protected."
3295,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He who associates someone with Allah will not be protected. This hadith has been narrated as marfu', hadith only by a narrator named Ishaq, according to one hadith he turned to it later."
3296,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The blood of the person for whom we are responsible will be (respectable) like our blood. Aban bin Taghlib has narrated a different tradition from this. He has narrated it with reference to Abu Junob along with his chain of transmission. The narrator named Abu Junob is a weak hadeeth."
3297,"Sayyiduna Ka'b bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: He intended to marry a Jewish (maybe the narrator has doubts) with a Christian woman. The narrator of this tradition, Abu Bakr bin Abu Maryam, is weak, while the other narrator, Ali bin Abu Talha, did not find the time of Sayyiduna Ka'b bin Malik."
3298,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When a Jew was killed with deceit, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered twelve thousand dirhams (as dowry) to be paid in this case."
3299,"Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Every contract (dhimmi) whether it is a Magian or someone else, its due date will be fulfilled."
3300,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) has also said the same thing."
3301,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: He found out the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Injuring an animal (or the death of a person as a result of it) will be futile, falling into a well and dying will be futile, falling into a mineral mine and dying, and payment of Khums will be required in Rakaz. A person asked him: O Abu Muhammad, was Abu Salama with him? So he said, If he had been with them, he would have been with them."
3302,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3303,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Injuring an animal (or the death of a person as a result of it) will be in vain, falling into a well and dying will be in vain, falling into a mineral mine and dying will be in vain, and payment of Khums will be required in Rakaz. Al-Zubaidi and Ja'far bin Burqan did not mention Abu Salamah in his chain of transmission."
3304,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Injuring an animal (or the death of a person as a result of it) will be in vain, falling into a well and dying, falling into a mineral mine and dying will be in vain, and payment of Khums will be required in Rakaz. Ibn Shihab states: The word used in this hadith, al-Jabbar, means his blood will be wasted and the word al-Ajma' means animal. Shaykh Abu Bakr Nishapuri says: According to my knowledge, no narrator except Yunus bin Yazid has mentioned that it was transmitted from Ubaidullah bin Abdullah in his chain of transmission."
3305,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By hitting the feet (of an animal) it will die."
3306,"The same tradition has been narrated along with another chain of transmission, but the names are not these words."
3307,"The same tradition is also narrated along with another document, however, it contains these words: He will burn in the fire and die."
3308,"Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal (may Allah have mercy on him) says about this hadith narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding Imam Abdul Razzaq (may Allah have mercy on him) that he will burn in the fire and go to die: It has no status and this hadith is not correct."
3309,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: It will be in vain to fall into the fire and die."
3310,"Narrated Hazeel: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""It will be useless to fall into a mineral mine and die, and it will be useless to die by falling into a well, it will be useless for a person to die (as a result of being killed by an animal), and it will be useless to die from (beating) the feet (of an animal), and in Raqqas, the payment of Khums will be required."""
3311,"Hazeel narrates on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah (may God be pleased with him): I believe that he, Marfu', has narrated it as a hadith."
3312,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said, “Injuring an animal (or causing a person to die) will be in vain, dying as a result of being trampled (by an animal) will be in vain, falling into a well and dying will be in vain, falling into a mineral mine and dying will be in vain, and the payment of Khums will be obligatory in Rakaz.”"
3313,"Haram bin Muhaisah narrates on the authority of his father: A camel of Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib entered someone's garden and damaged some things there, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed that the protection of property (i.e. land and gardens) during the day is the responsibility of their owners, and the protection of animals during the night is the responsibility of their (animal) owners. Wahib and Abu Mas'ud al-Jajj have differed somewhat in the transmission of Muammar, they did not mention it as a transmission of his father."
3314,"Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: An Ansari camel entered a garden and caused damage, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed that the owners of the gardens are responsible for their protection during the day, while the owners of the cattle will be responsible for the young animals causing damage at night. Yunus narrates: Shafi'i heard this hadith from Ayyub, but he narrated it on the authority of Zuhri, on the authority of Haram, on the authority of Sayyidna Bara'."
3315,"Haram bin Muhaisa narrates on the authority of his father: Sayyidna Bara bin Azib (RA) says: The camel of Sayyidna Bara (RA) entered a garden."
3316,"Haram bin Muhaisah narrates on the authority of Bara bin Azib (may God be pleased with him): He had a she-camel that damaged (someone's garden). After that, he has mentioned the previous hadith regarding the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Faryabi, Ayyub bin Khalid, and other hadith scholars have disagreed in quoting it with reference to Imam Uza'i."
3317,"Haram bin Muhaisah narrates on the authority of Sayyidna Bara bin Azib: When a camel of the family of Sayyidna Bara damaged something, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled that the protection of fruits (i.e. gardens and produce) during the day is the responsibility of their owners, and the owners of cattle will pay for what the harmful cattle damage at night."
3318,"Haram bin Muhaisa narrates on the authority of Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib, may Allah be pleased with him, the camel of these people."
3319,"Narrated Haram bin Saad bin Muhaisah: The camel of Sayyiduna Bara entered a garden and damaged (the produce) there. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was complained about. This tradition is also narrated along with some other isnads."
3320,"Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Azhar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: On the occasion of the Battle of Hunain, I saw the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passing through the people. Sayyidna Khalid bin Waleed (may Allah be pleased with him) was inquiring about the place of Qiyam. threw Then a drunken person was brought before Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) and he punished him with forty lashes."
3321,"Ibn Wabara Kalbi narrates: Sayyidna Khalid bin Waleed (RA) sent me to Sayyidna Umar (RA). He says that when I arrived at the service of Sayyidna Umar (RA), at that time Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA), Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, Sayyidna Ali, Sayyidna Talha (RA) and Sayyidna Zubair (RA) were also present. They were all reclining in the mosque. I said: I have been sent to serve you. They greeted you: Yes, and requested this: People have started drinking too much and they do not pay any attention to its punishment. Sayyiduna Umar said: These men are here before you. Ask them about this. Hazrat Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said that what he (Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: He should convey it to his master (sayyedna Khalid bin Waleed (may Allah be pleased with him)). The narrator narrates: When a weak person who had committed this crime was brought before Sayyiduna Umar, he used to give him forty lashes."
3322,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3323,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3324,"Sayyidina Abd al-Rahman bin Azhar (RA) narrates: On the occasion of the Battle of Hunain, a man was brought before the Prophet (PBUH) who had drunk alcohol, and the Prophet (PBUH) told the people to beat him, so the people gathered and beat him with their shoes."
3325,"Abdullah bin Abd al-Rahman bin Azhar narrates the following statement from his father: A man was brought to the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who had been drinking alcohol. The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was present in Hunain at that time. He threw dirt on his face and ordered his companions to beat him with their shoes and whatever they had in their hands until (after some time) the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: Stop now, then he People stopped. This was the method (of punishing drunkards) until the death of Prophet Reem (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). After that, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) imposed forty lashes as punishment for drinking alcohol, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) imposed forty lashes in the early part of his caliphate and started imposing eighty lashes in the last part. Retained the same whips."
3326,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A maidservant of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave birth to a child as a result of adultery. When it becomes pure, issuing a limit on it. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also said: Set a limit (on the slaves and maidservants) under your possession. Shu'ba, Israel, Shareek, Ibrahim ibn Tahman, and Abu Waqiyyah have followed in quoting it from Abd al-Ali."
3327,"Abu Abd al-Rahman narrates: Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said while giving a sermon: O people! Fear Allah, and if your slaves or maidservants commit adultery, flog them, whether they are free or not, because a slave girl of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) committed this crime, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to flog her. If I flog her, she will die. I returned to the service of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) and mentioned this to him. I said: O Prophet of Allah, if I beat her, I am afraid she will die."
3328,"Abu Abd al-Rahman narrates: I heard Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) making a similar mention of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but it contained these words, so I left the slave girl until she was cured and recovered."
3329,"Sayyidina Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man's slave girl commits adultery, a man should flog her and verbally call her a brana. (Here the narrator is in doubt as to which word has been used for rope, habul, yazfir)."
3330,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3331,"The same tradition is also narrated along with another document, but in it he did not state that he had narrated this tradition with reference to his father."
3332,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3333,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3334,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “When a man’s maid commits adultery, he should flog her according to the command of the Book of Allah and verbally call her ‘Branah’. If she does it again, then do the same thing again. Sell it."
3335,"This tradition is also narrated along with another document."
3336,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) said, “When a man’s slave-girl commits adultery and is found guilty of adultery, that person should flog her as a limit, but verbally call her ‘Branah’ (the narrator says). The word used in this hadith, Zafir, refers to a rope."
3337,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: Walubanqid min shayar, (here the meaning of naqid is also rope)."
3338,"Amr ibn Shuaib, on the authority of his father, narrates this statement of his grandfather: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “There shall be no cursing between four types of people: a free man, (husband) and a slave girl (there shall be no cursing between the wife and husband), a free woman (wife) and a slave (there shall be no cursing between the husband), a Muslim (husband) and a Jew (wife), and there shall be no cursing between a Muslim (husband) and a Christian (wife). A narrator named Uthman bin Abd al-Rahman is a Waqasi and hadiths are obsolete."
3339,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said, “There shall be no cursing between four types of women (and their husbands): a Christian woman who is the wife of a Muslim, a Jewish woman who is the wife of a Muslim, a slave girl who is the wife of a free man, and a free woman who is the wife of a slave. There are Khorasanis named Uthman bin Ata and they are very weak. The narrator named Yazid bin Bazi Ramli has quoted it with reference to Ata, but they are also weak. This hadith has been narrated on the authority of Imam Uza'i and Ibn Juraj on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib on the authority of his father on the authority of his grandfather on the authority of his grandfather."
3340,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather, regarding his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: (and quoted it as his own saying: he did not quote it as a hadith). It is narrated along with another chain of transmission: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may God be pleased with him) says: There will be no curse between such women and their husbands: a Jewish woman who is the wife of a Muslim, a Christian woman who is the wife of a Muslim, a free woman who is the wife of a slave, and a woman who is the wife of a free person."
3341,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather, regarding his father: The Prophet (peace be upon him) sent Sayyiduna Utaab ibn Asayd (he then narrates the same hadith as before). The narrators of this tradition are Hamad bin Amr, Ammar bin Matar and Zayd bin Rafi'."
3342,"Qabaisa bin Zuhaib narrates: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) scolded a man who had intercourse with one of his slave girls who was the wife of a slave, and the slave did not divorce him. Sayyidna Umar (RA) gave a ruling about a person who first denied having a child (of his own) by a woman while the child was still in the woman's womb, then he confessed, and the child was still in the woman's womb. When the child was born, the man refused it again, so Sayyiduna Umar (RA) ordered that he should be flogged (as Huddaqf) for what he had accused the woman of, and Sayyidna Umar (RA) established the lineage of the child with that woman."
3343,"Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) says: If a person commits a punishable crime and I impose a limit on him and he dies because of it, I consider that I have to pay his dowry, except for a person who has been permitted to drink alcohol, because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not prescribe anything (regular) about this."
3344,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: During the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), those who drank alcohol were beaten with hands, shoes and sticks, until the Prophet (may God’s prayers and peace be upon him) passed away. Sayyidna Umar also gave forty lashes to those who drank alcohol, until a Sahab from the first emigrants who had drunk alcohol was brought before Sayyidna Umar, who had drunk alcohol, and he was ordered to flog him. So he said: Allah has said this in His Book: ""Those who believe and do righteous deeds, there will be no sin on them for what they eat and drink."" (He said) I am among those who believed, did good deeds, became pious and became believers, then became pious and did good (which is mentioned in the Qur'an). I was with the Holy Prophet in the Battle of Badr, the Battle of Uhud, the Battle of Khandaq and all other battles. Sayyiduna Umar said to the other people, ""Why don't you answer what he said?"" So Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas said: This verse was revealed as an excuse for the past people as a proof against the hypocrites, because Allah said: O you who believe, indeed, wine and gambling. Al-Sayyidna Ibn Abbas read these two verses in full and said: If these are among the people who believed and did good deeds, then Allah has forbidden them to drink alcohol. Sayyidna Umar (RA) said: You are right. And when delusion spreads, he makes a false accusation of adultery, and the one who falsely accuses of adultery is given the same whipping, so according to the order of Sayyiduna Umar, he was given the same whipping."
3345,"Narrated Sa'ib bin Yazid: He was with Sayyiduna Umar when he flogged the person who smelled of alcohol."
3346,"Sa'ib bin Yazid narrates: Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) whipped a person and he smelled alcohol from that person."
3347,"Sayyiduna Anas Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: A Jewish person passed by a girl who was wearing an ornament, he (took off that ornament and injured the girl) and threw it into a well. He said that such and such a Jew was brought to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he confessed his crime, so he was also killed under the order of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
3348,"Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: A Jew killed a girl by taking away her jewelry, and this Jew stoned her to death. When the girl was brought to the Prophet (PBUH), there was life in her. He nodded his head in response and said: No. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then asked him again whether so-and-so killed you. So he answered with a nod of his head, yes, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put the head of this Jew between two stones and killed him by crushing it in between."
3349,"The same tradition is narrated along with another document, however, Qatadah has quoted these words in his tradition, this Jew had confessed his crime."
3350,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a Jew injured an Ansari girl by taking off her necklace and threw her into a pit and crushed her head with a stone, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that if she (the Jew) should be stoned to death, she should be stoned."
3351,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person committed adultery and was flogged as punishment under the order of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
3352,"Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: A man committed adultery with a woman, and he was flogged as punishment under the order of the Prophet (SAW)."
3353,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, narrates: Once the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was giving a sermon to the people on Friday. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Sit down.” He sat down, then he stood up for the third time. The person belonging to Banwalith was not married. It was asked, O Messenger of Allah, why don't you flog the woman with whom he has committed a sin? The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said, ""Flog her, then bring her to me."" He replied, ""Such and such a woman. He mentioned the name of a woman belonging to Banubakar. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called this woman and asked her about it. She said: She lied: ""By Allah, I do not even know her, and I am innocent of what she has accused me of, and Allah is witness to what I am saying."" because this woman denies that you have committed any sin with her. If you have any proof, I will flog her, and if you have no proof, I will flog her as a punishment for making a false accusation of adultery."
3354,"Saeed Ibn Musaib narrates: When Sayyiduna Umar (RA) performed the Hajj for the last time, after which he did not get the chance to perform Hajj, during that Hajj, a Muslim man was found dead in the residential area of Banu Da'ah. Sayyidna Umar (RA) sent a message to him. So they answered no. Sayyiduna Umar took fifty thousand of them, and made them stand in Hatim, and took this oath from them: (That they should take this oath) By Allah, who is the Lord of this sacred house, the Lord of this sacred city, the Lord of this sacred month, you people did not kill him, and you do not even know about his killer, these people took this oath, when these people took this oath. Then Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said, ""Either you pay this person's Dayat Mughlaza in terms of camels, pay a full Dayat in terms of Dirhams and Dinar, and pay one-third of the Dayat (amount of money)."" So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""No, I have given a decision about you according to the decision of your Prophet."" So these people paid a full diyat according to dinars and chose to pay a third of the diyat (amount). The narrator of this hadith is Umar bin Subhbi."
3355,"Saeed bin Musayyib narrates: Sayyiduna Umar, may God be pleased with him, fixed the diet of a Jew and a Christian at four thousand dirhams and the diet of a Magian at eight hundred dirhams."
3356,"Saeed bin Musayyib narrates: Sayyiduna Umar, may God be pleased with him, fixed the diet of a Jew and a Christian at four thousand dirhams and the diet of a Magian at eight hundred dirhams."
3357,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person was brought to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who had become intoxicated due to the consumption of dates, so the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flogged him."
3358,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared the diet of two members of the tribe of Amir to be equal to the diet of a Muslim. Shaykh Abu Bakr says: That is, each of them had the religion of a Muslim, while both of them were dhimmis."
3359,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made the diet of the People of the Book half of the diet of the Muslim. Ibn Wahhib has quoted these words: The diet of a disbeliever is set as half of the diet of a Muslim."
3360,"Amr ibn Shuaib, on the authority of his father, narrates the statement of his grandfather: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, has decreed: The diet of both types of People of the Book (i.e. Jews and Christians) will be as much as the diet of Muslims, (says the narrator) meaning Jews and Christians."
3361,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) says: There will be five types (of camels) in the slaughtering of camels."
3362,"This tradition is narrated along with another document. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) says: There will be five types of (camels) in the day of slaughtering (camels)."
3363,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3364,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decided to pay one hundred camels as compensation for murder, out of which twenty would be Haqqah and twenty would be Jaza’a, twenty would be women of Lubun, twenty would be women in labor and twenty would be women of Khad. Sahibzada Abu Ubaidah has narrated it with a valid chain of transmission, which cannot be discredited, and this tradition cannot be interpreted. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) was very fearing of his Lord and was very firm in his religion. It cannot be expected of him that he would narrate a hadith regarding the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) had given this decision and then issue a fatwa against it. I have not heard anything from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this and I do not know of any tradition regarding the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I will present my opinion in this matter, if it is right, it will be from Allah and His Messenger, and if there is a mistake in it, it will be from me. His companions saw that he was so happy that the fatwa given by him was in accordance with the decision of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. His companions had never seen him so happy. So how can this be true about those who have this attribute and this condition, that they narrate a hadith regarding the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then contradict it (saw fatwa). This is also supported by the tradition which was narrated by Abu Ubaidah, the son of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, and this tradition was narrated by Waqi’, Abdullah bin Wahib and other muhaddiths, with reference to Sufyan Al-Thawri Mansoor, Ibrahim Nakhai, about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with them."
3365,"The judge narrated it to us - the judge al-Mahamili narrated it to us, Al-'Abbas ibn Yazid narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Abdullah, who said: ""The blood-money for manslaughter is in fifths,"" then he explained it exactly as Abu 'Ubaydah and 'Alqamah explained it on his authority. This report, even though it contains an interruption (irsal), Ibrahim al-Nakha'i is the person most knowledgeable about 'Abdullah, his opinion, and his rulings, having taken this from his maternal uncles 'Alqamah, al-Aswad, and 'Abd al-Rahman - the two sons of Yazid - and others among the senior companions of 'Abdullah. He is the one who said: ""When I say to you, 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said,' it is from a group of his companions on his authority, but when I hear it from a single man, I name him to you.""

And another point: the elevated (marfu') report which mentions ""sons of makhad"" - we do not know of anyone who narrated it except Khishf ibn Malik, from Ibn Mas'ud, and he is an unknown man. No one narrated it from him except Zayd ibn Jubayr ibn Harmal al-Jushami. The people of knowledge in hadith do not accept as proof a report narrated solely by a man who is not well-known; rather, knowledge is established for them by a report only when its narrators are either a well-known trustworthy person, or a man from whom the designation of ""unknown"" has been lifted. The lifting of the designation of ""unknown"" from him occurs when two or more men narrate from him. When this is his description, the designation of ""unknown"" is lifted from him and he then becomes known. But as for one from whom only a single man has narrated, being the sole narrator of a report, it is obligatory to withhold judgment regarding that report of his until someone else corroborates him. And Allah knows best.

And another point: regarding the report of Khishf ibn Malik, we do not know that anyone narrated it from Zayd ibn Jubayr on his authority except Hajjaj ibn Artah, and Hajjaj is a man well-known for tadlis (concealment in transmission) and for narrating from those he never met and from those he never heard from. Abu Mu'awiyah al-Darir said: Hajjaj said to me, ""Let no one ask me about the report"" - meaning: when I narrate something to you, do not ask me who informed you of it. And Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah said: I was with Hajjaj ibn Artah one day, and he ordered the door to be closed, then said: ""I did not hear anything from al-Zuhri, and I did not hear from Ibrahim, nor from al-Sha'bi except one hadith, nor from so-and-so, nor from so-and-so"" - until he counted seventeen or more than ten, all of whom Hajjaj had narrated from. Then, after narrating from them, he claimed that he had never met them nor heard from them. Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan, and 'Isa ibn Yunus abandoned narrating from him after having sat with him and come to know him - and that they did so is sufficient proof of their knowledge and excellence regarding men. Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah said: ""I visited Hajjaj ibn Artah and heard his speech, and he mentioned something I found objectionable, so I did not carry anything from him."" Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan said: ""I saw Hajjaj ibn Artah in Makkah, and I did not carry anything from him, nor did I carry anything from a man who narrated from him, whom I considered unreliable (mudtarib)."" Yahya ibn Ma'in said: ""Hajjaj ibn Artah's hadith is not to be relied upon."" 'Abdullah ibn Idris said: ""I heard Hajjaj say, 'A man does not attain nobility until he abandons the congregational prayer.'"" 'Isa ibn Yunus said: ""I heard Hajjaj say, 'I go out to prayer and the porters and greengrocers jostle me.'"" Jarir said: ""I heard Hajjaj say, 'Love of wealth and status has destroyed me.'""

And another point: a group of trustworthy narrators transmitted this hadith from Hajjaj ibn Artah, but they differed among themselves regarding it. 'Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated it from Hajjaj with the wording we have mentioned from him, and 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad agreed with him on that. But Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi - who is among the trustworthy - differed from both of them, narrating it from Hajjaj, from Zayd ibn Jubayr, from Khishf ibn Malik, who said: I heard 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud say: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ruled concerning manslaughter that it be in fifths: twenty four-year-old she-camels, twenty five-year-old she-camels giving milk, twenty three-year-old male camels giving milk, twenty two-year-old she-camels, and twenty two-year-old male camels"" - placing, in place of the four-year-old camels (hiqaq), the three-year-old male camels giving milk (bani labun)."
3366,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave this decision in the case of killing a sin, it will consist of five types of camels, one type, Jazaa, one type of Haqqah, one type of female Lubun, one type of female Mukhad and one type of male, Banulbon. He has mentioned Banulbon instead of Banumkhaud."
3367,"This hadith has been narrated by Ahmad bin Muhammad and other narrators along with their chain of transmission, with reference to Khushf bin Malik, the statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prescribed the payment of five types of camels for the death of a person who commits a sin. Apart from this, these gentlemen did not copy the word and did not copy the sentence explaining these five types."
3368,"Muhammad bin Qasim Zakariya has narrated this tradition on the authority of Hisham bin Yunus, on the authority of Abu Malik Junbi. All these gentlemen have narrated this hadith regarding Hajj. Ismail bin Muhammad Safar has narrated this tradition from Hajjaj on the authority of Saadan bin Nasr on the authority of Abu Muawiya. Abu Bakr Nishapuri has narrated it on the authority of Abu Muawiya on the authority of Muhammad bin Yazid Tafur. Ahmad bin Najda has narrated a tradition similar to that of Hafs on the authority of Hamani and Abu Muawiya on the authority of him. This hadith has been narrated by Yahya bin Zakariya bin Abu Zayda with reference to Hajjaj, then there has been a dispute with him regarding the copying. Sirih bin Yunus adapted Abd al-Rahim and Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad. Abu Hisham Rifa'i has narrated a different tradition from this. He has narrated it in agreement with Abu Mu'awiyah Zarir and those who follow him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has prescribed the Dayat (payment of camels) in five parts. As you have seen, there is a difference in this narration regarding the Hajjaj, as you have seen, so there may be a possibility that it is authentically proven from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) prescribed the payment of camels in the day of killing a sin) in five categories, as Abu Muawiya, Hafs, Abu Malik Junbi, Abu Khalid, Ibn Abi Zaida in the narration narrated by Abu Hisham mentioned these five. The description of the types has not been copied, it is agreed upon by all these gentlemen, their number is also high and all of them are trustworthy. Here is also a possibility: the narrator named Hajjaj sometimes explains the five types as his opinion after narrating the hadith of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), which gives the listener the illusion that this may also be a part of the hadith of the Prophet, even though those words are not part of the hadith, but are the words of Hajjaj. This possibility is strengthened by the fact that Abdul Wahid bin Ziyad, Abdul Rahim and Yahya bin Saeed Umayyad have disagreed in quoting traditions regarding him, as we have already mentioned the traditions of these gentlemen, that Yahya bin Saeed Umayyad has mentioned twenty Banulbon instead of Bes, Haqqa, while Abdul Wahid and Abdul Rahim have quoted the words of Beis Haqq instead of Banulbon, Allah knows best. One aspect of it is this: Various sayings have been narrated about a group of Companions belonging to the Muhajireen Ansar of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the issue of the deed of murder, and according to our knowledge, none of them mention Binumkhadh in this tradition. As far as the hadith transmitted from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is concerned, it was narrated by Ishaq bin Yahya bin Waleed bin Ubadah on the authority of Sayyidina Ubadah bin Samit (may God be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace be upon him). This hadith is transmitted by Ishaq bin Yahya. He has not heard the hadiths from Sayyidna Ubadah bin Samit. Amr bin Shoaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, ""Whoever is killed for committing a crime, his death will be one hundred camels, of which thirty will be female, thirty will be male, thirty will be right, and ten will be male."
3369,"There are two possibilities in this hadith, one aspect is: Amr bin Shuaib did not mention in it that his father heard the hadith from his grandfather Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may God be pleased with him) (or not). A similar tradition has been narrated about Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) that Ishaq Bin Yahya has narrated regarding Sayyidna Ubadah (RA). Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) say: In the death of a person who commits a crime, there will be thirty righteous, thirty daughters will be Lubun, twenty daughters will be pregnant, and twenty males will be Banu Lubun."
3370,"This same hadith along with another chain of transmission is related to Sayyidna Uthman and Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (RA)."
3371,"The same hadith along with another chain of transmission is related to Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (RA)."
3372,"It is narrated about Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that: He says, four kinds of camels (will be paid) in the day of killing Khata: twenty-five, Jiza'a, twenty-five Haqqa, twenty-five Labun daughters, and twenty-five Makhad daughters."
3373,"The same hadith along with another chain of transmission is related to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) and the same is related to Imam Shaabi and Ibrahim Nakhai."
3374,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The death penalty for the murder of a person will be paid in the form of four types of (camels), twenty-five will be Haqqah, twenty-five will be Jazaa, twenty-five daughters will be Laboon, and twenty-five daughters will be Makhad."
3375,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever kills someone intentionally will be entrusted to the guardian of the deceased, and if they want, they can kill him, and if they want, they can receive a dowry, which will be thirty, right, thirty jaza'a, forty caliphs."
3376,"Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: In cases of willful murder, reconciliation and confession, the family will not pay dowry."
3377,"Sha'bi states: The family shall not be responsible for the payment of a slave, murder (of a murderer), reconciliation, (payment determined as) and acknowledgment (of any payment on their part)."
3378,"Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: Do not charge the family with any part of a person who confesses."
3379,"Narrated by Sayyidna Hazail bin Shahrabeel (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood of a person who dies falling into a mineral (mine) will be wasted, the blood of a person who warms in a well will be wasted, the blood of a person who dies from being killed by an animal will be wasted, the payment of Khums will be required in Raqqa, and the blood of a person who dies from being kicked by an animal will be wasted. are: This blood shall be in vain."
3380,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3381,"Sayyidna Huzail (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The blood of the foot (of the animal) will be wasted. This hadith is transmitted."
3382,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3383,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""The blood of the foot (of the animal) will be wasted."""
3384,"The same hadith is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: The blood of the person who dies from being killed by an animal will be wasted, the blood of the person who is heated in a well will be wasted, the blood of the person who dies in a mineral (mine) will be wasted."
3385,"Narrated by Sayyidna Nu'man bin Basheer (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said, ""Whoever keeps his animal in the way of the Muslims or in the bazaar, and that animal tramples someone under his hand or foot, then that person will be a guarantor."""
3386,"Sayyidah Umm Sulaiman Shafaa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) appointed Sayyiduna Abu Jaham bin Ghanim (RA) to be the custodian of the booty on the occasion of the Battle of Hunain."
3387,"Amir (Shaabi) narrated: A thief was brought to Sayyiduna Ali (RA) who had stolen, and Sayyidna Ali (RA) cut off his hand. For stealing again, he was brought again, and Sayyidna Ali (RA) cut off his foot. It can eat something and absorb it."
3388,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When a thief steals, I will cut off his right hand; if he does it again, I will cut off his left foot; if he does it again, I will keep him in prison until he recovers, because I am ashamed to leave him in such a state (after that he mentioned according to the previous hadith)."
3389,"Sayyidina Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: A thief was brought to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and the Prophet (PBUH) cut off his hand. Katwadiya, he was then accused of theft and was killed under the order of the Holy Prophet."
3390,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3391,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3392,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace: When a thief steals, cut off his hand; if he does it again, cut off his foot; if he does it again, cut off his hand; if he does it again, cut off his foot. Khalid bin Salamah has narrated this tradition in the same way, while other narrators have narrated it on the authority of his uncle Harith on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him)."
3393,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I was present with Sayyidna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), he cut off one of his (thief's) hands and one of his feet (already)."
3394,"Sha'bi narrated: Two men brought a man to Sayyiduna Ali, they both testified about this person that he had stolen. Sayyidna Ali cut off his hand, then those two men brought another person and said: The first time we made a mistake, this is the real thief. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If I had known that you had deliberately cut off the hands of the first person, I would have cut off both of your hands."
3395,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: When a limit is issued to a thief, he will not be obliged to pay the ransom (for the stolen property)."
3396,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When a limit is issued to a thief, then he will not be obliged to pay the ransom (for the stolen property)."
3397,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When a limit is issued to a thief, then he will not be obliged to pay the ransom (for the stolen property)."
3398,"The same hadith has been narrated from Sayyidina Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, may Allah be pleased with him, with reference to some other isnads, in which there has been a dispute about a narrator and he has been declared anonymous, and the possibility that this hadith may have been transmitted has been indicated."
3399,"Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A thief was brought to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his hand to be cut off and said that he will not pay the ransom."
3400,"Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a limit is issued to a thief, he will not be obliged to pay the ransom (for the stolen property)."
3401,"Narrated by Nafi: A person who had one hand and one foot amputated (as a punishment for theft) became a guest of Sayyidna Abu Bakr Siddique RA. He replied, ""Ya'li bin Maniya has cut it as a cruel act."" Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) said to him, ""I will write to him about it."" Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) promised him. Found by the pass, when his research revealed that he had been sold by the same amputee. The narrator narrates: Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Radiyallahu Anhu said: By Allah, what is more severe (unpleasant) to me than this action of his is that he was praying to Allah (that the thief be caught), you people cut off his foot (so that he will not be able to do anything with his hand)."
3402,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) narrated: Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) cut off the foot of the person whose hand was cut off by Ya'li Ibn Umayyah."
3403,"Sayyida Aisha (RA) narrates: A black man came to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) and stayed with him. Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) began to teach him the Qur'an. But he did not agree to this, so Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) sent him along with the receiver, and urged him to take care of (the black person). After some time, the (black) person came and his hand was cut. When Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) saw him, tears flowed from Tawan's eyes. I was responsible for one of his duties (i.e. an animal or something) and he cut off my hand, then Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) said, ""The one who cut off his hand has betrayed more than twenty duties, by Allah!"" If you are right, then I will imprison him for that reason. Then Sayyidna Abu Bakr kept him with him and treated him as before. The man stood up at night (during the Nawafil), and when Sayyidna Abu Bakr heard his voice, he prayed, ""O Allah, punish the one who cut his hand."" Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Last night, there was a theft with us. He stood up with a severed hand (black). He turned towards the Qiblah. He raised both his right hand and the severed hand and prayed: O Allah, catch him who has stolen this (or use similar words). Muammar Nai, the narrator, narrated these words: (The black man prayed:) May Allah catch the person who stole from this noble house. The narrator narrates: The day was not even half over, that the goods were found with this person, and Sayyidna Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, said to him. The foot was amputated."
3404,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: When Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) heard his voice, he said, ""You do not spend the night of a thief."""
3405,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I bear witness that Sayyidna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) cut off the foot of a person who had stolen for the third time, before having one hand and one foot cut off."
3406,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had his hand amputated (for stealing) something worth five dirhams."
3407,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3408,"Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Five (fingers i.e. hands) will be cut off for five (theft of an item worth dirhams)."
3409,"Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Five (fingers i.e. hands) will be cut off for five (theft of an item worth dirhams)."
3410,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off his hand for stealing an item worth five dirhams. A narrator named Abu Hilal narrates: Some narrators told me: Ibn Abu Arooba narrated this hadith from Sayyidna Anas Radiyallahu Anhu from Sayyidna Abu Bakr Radiyallahu Anhu. Abu Hilal says: If it is not narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding Sayyiduna Anas, then it is either transmitted from the Prophet or it will be from Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him)."
3411,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The hand of a person who cheats, takes bribes, and commits robbery (in public) will not be cut off."
3412,"Abdullah Bin Amr Hazrami narrates: I brought my slave to Sayyiduna Umar Bin Khattab, I said: O Commander of the Faithful, cut off his hand. Sayyidna Umar asked what he has done. I said: He has stolen my wife's mirror, which was worth more than sixty dirhams, then Sayyiduna Umar said: Your servant has stolen your belongings, his hand will not be cut off."
3413,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: She heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: Breaking the bone of a dead person is as sinful as breaking the bone of a living person."
3414,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Breaking the bone of a dead Muslim is like breaking the bone of a living person."
